    "Cut the cards in the middle. Partner A takes the left half, Partner B takes the right half.",
    "A builds question 1 from the tiles and asks it: \"What did you eat for dinner yesterday?\" (You add did.)",
    "B hears the question and builds the answer in the past simple. Regular verbs add -ed (work → worked). Many common verbs are irregular (go → went). A tile \"not\" means didn't.",
    "Then B asks question 2 and A answers. Take turns. At the end, check with the answer sheet.",
    "Last, swap cards and do it all again, faster."
